From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Panther X2 User <user@example.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: enable MPP, NPU and RGA for
 rk3566-panther-x2

Enable the following hardware blocks on Panther X2:
- MPP (Media Process Platform) for video encode/decode
- NPU (Neural Processing Unit) for AI inference
- RGA (Raster Graphics Acceleration) for 2D graphics / colorspace conversion

These nodes are defined in rk356x.dtsi with status = "disabled" by default.
Enable them so that /dev/mpp_service, /dev/dri/renderD129 (NPU), and /dev/rga
are available when using the rk35xx BSP kernel.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-panther-x2.dts | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-panther-x2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-panther-x2.dts
@@ -430,3 +430,24 @@
 &usb_host0_ehci {
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&bus_npu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mpp_srv {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&rknpu {
+	rknpu-supply = <&vdd_npu>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&rknpu_mmu {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&rk_rga {
+	status = "okay";
+};
